{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788202314,"nonce":"h0jATFiIDSePiVVtWe4t0hHsDFA=","message":"VERIFICATION (backlog verification pass, git-bug 2f2796e, run fbb2c59)\n\nCORRECTED — one item in the WHAT IS MISSING list is already shipped, and it is\nthe one the whole design turns on. Plus a modal force-pause and a red-error path\nsitting on the exact write this issue exists to add. The issue is correctly\nself-declared as a placeholder rather than a spec, so there is no acceptance\nsection to assess — but three facts below must land in it when it is written up.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 1 — \"ANYTHING THAT BUILDS OR RECOGNISES A PRISON ROOM\" IS MISSING:\nRECOGNITION ALREADY SHIPS. ONLY BUILDING DOES NOT.\n=====================================================================\n\n`Source/AutoRimmer/PlaceVerbs.Brief` — which feeds BOTH `rooms` and `room` —\nalready publishes per room:\n\n    [\"role\"] = role?.defName,\n    [\"role_label\"] = role?.label,\n    ...\n    [\"prison_cell\"] = room.IsPrisonCell,\n\nand `PlaceVerbs.CheapScore` even ranks prison cells up the `rooms` list\n(`if (r.IsPrisonCell) score += 20000;`). `room \u003cid\u003e` additionally reports\n`[\"for_prisoners\"] = ... bed.ForPrisoners` per bed. And `room.Role` will report\n`PrisonCell` / `PrisonBarracks` because `RimWorld/RoomRoleDefOf` declares both.\n\nSo **\"is there a prison?\" — the deterministic world fact this issue and\n`cc8988c` both say the finish-off policy turns on — is answerable TODAY**, from\n`rooms`. That is the single largest correction here: the issue's \"started from\nnothing\" framing undersells the mod by one whole half of the feature, and\n`cc8988c`'s acceptance bullet \"defaulting on only while no prison exists\" is\ntherefore runnable now rather than blocked.\n\nCONFIRMED as genuinely missing: prisoner BED assignment. Greps over\n`Source/AutoRimmer/` for `ForPrisoners|Building_Bed|ForOwnerType|CompAssignableToPawn|ownership\\.`\nreturn only reads and gates — `PlaceVerbs`' report, `PawnEmergencyVerbs`' bed\ngate (`else if (bed.ForPrisoners || !bed.Medical)`), `PawnOrderVerbs`'\n`TakeToBedGate`/`FindBed` search, and a cast in `MedicalBillVerbs`. **Nothing\nwrites `ForPrisoners` or `ForOwnerType`, and nothing assigns a bed owner.**\n`assign` is policies/area/medcare only — its own error text enumerates the whole\nsurface. CONFIRMED.\n\nAlso CONFIRMED missing: recruitment campaign logic. A case-insensitive grep for\n`recruit` outside `WardenVerbs.cs` returns zero. One corollary the issue does not\nstate: `PawnSerializer.Guest` publishes `resistance` and `will` but NOT\n`recruitable` — only `WardenVerbs.GuestLine` does. A campaign playbook reading\n`pawn \u003cid\u003e` cannot see whether a prisoner is recruitable at all.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 2 — THE PRISON-BED WRITE HAS A FORCE-PAUSE MODAL AND A RED ERROR ON\nIT, AND NEITHER IS IN THE ISSUE\n=====================================================================\n\nThis is the whole write the issue proposes to add, so it is worth stating in\nfull before anyone specs it.\n\n**(a) `Building_Bed.ForPrisoners = false` EMITS A RED ERROR.** Verbatim from the\nsetter:\n\n    forOwnerType = BedOwnerType.Colonist;\n    Log.Error(\"Bed ForPrisoners=false, but should it be for for colonists or slaves?  Set ForOwnerType instead.\");\n\nSo any \"un-prison this bed\" verb that writes the obvious property breaches the\nzero-red-errors invariant on its FIRST call. Write `ForOwnerType` instead. (There\nis a second `Log.Error` in the same setter for `Current.ProgramState != Playing`,\nand it silently early-returns for `ForHumanBabies` and non-`bed_humanlike` defs.)\n\n**(b) The player's own route is a `Dialog_MessageBox`, i.e. a force-pause wedge.**\n`Building_Bed.GetGizmos` routes the prisoner toggle to\n`Building_Bed.SetBedOwnerTypeByInterface`, which ends:\n\n    Find.WindowStack.Add(Dialog_MessageBox.CreateConfirmation(stringBuilder.ToString(), action));\n\n`Dialog_MessageBox` sets `forcePause = true`, so per 1.7/1.8 that halts every\nsubsequent `advance` at 0 ticks until 3.5 ships. This is DESIGN's 2026-08-31\n\"dangerous shape\" — a modal on a utility's own execution path — and the grep that\nfinds it is `new Dialog_MessageBox`, exactly as that entry prescribes.\n\nTwo further reasons the same method is unusable from a verb regardless:\n  * it computes its affected-bed set from the UI SELECTION —\n    `foreach (Building_Bed item in Find.Selector.SelectedObjects.OfType\u003cBuilding_Bed\u003e())`\n    — which is empty on an unattended bench;\n  * `if (lastBedOwnerSetChangeFrame == Time.frameCount) { return; }` — a per-frame\n    debounce, so a BATCH verb setting several beds in one frame silently no-ops\n    after the first. That is a false positive of the `4087644` class.\n  * and the action silently OVERRIDES the request:\n    `if (ownerType == BedOwnerType.Prisoner \u0026\u0026 room2.TouchesMapEdge) { item2.ForOwnerType = BedOwnerType.Colonist; }`\n    — a map-edge room cannot be a prison and the game does not say so.\n\n**The precedent for the right handling already exists in this repo and nobody has\napplied it here.** `PawnOrderVerbs`' `[Verb(\"arrest\")]` faces the identical shape\n— `FloatMenuOptionProvider_Arrest`'s action ends in\n`TutorUtility.DoModalDialogIfNotKnown(ConceptDefOf.ArrestingCreatesEnemies, ...)`\n-\u003e `new Dialog_MessageBox` — and it does not call the delegate; it reproduces the\ngate, takes the job itself, and drops the tutorial line. The bed verb must do the\nsame: re-implement the bed-set computation, write `ForOwnerType` directly, and\ncall `Notify_RoomShapeOrContainedBedsChanged` itself. Under Ideology the widget is\na different one again (`Command_SetBedOwnerType`), so the gate is a union.\n\n=====================================================================\nCONFIRMED — WHAT ALREADY SHIPS IS MORE THAN THE ISSUE SAYS\n=====================================================================\n\n- `warden` — CONFIRMED and the argument list is UNDERSTATED. `WardenVerbs.cs`'s\n  own signature comment is\n  `warden {pawns:[…], mode?, enable?:[…], disable?:[…], slave_mode?, recruitable?, convert_to?}`\n  — the issue omits `slave_mode` and `clear`. The exclusive/non-exclusive split is\n  honoured and cited\n  (`if (mode != null \u0026\u0026 mode.isNonExclusiveInteraction) throw new VerbArgsException(...)`),\n  and vanilla backs it both ways: `Pawn_GuestTracker.SetExclusiveInteraction` and\n  `ToggleNonExclusiveInteraction` each `Log.ErrorOnce` when handed the other kind.\n  `Release` is a mode by construction and the result payload says so.\n- `dev:guest-status` — CONFIRMED, and there is a SECOND staging route the issue\n  misses: `PawnFixtureVerbs.Prisoner` (the `prisoner` step of `pawn-fixture`)\n  generates a pawn from nothing and calls\n  `pawn.guest.SetGuestStatus(faction, GuestStatus.Prisoner);`. The bench can stage\n  a prisoner without an existing pawn to convert.\n- `arrest` and `capture` shipped in 3.4 — CONFIRMED\n  (`[Verb(\"capture\")] ... =\u003e TakeToBed(ctx, \"capture\");`, same for arrest).\n- The prisoner classifier — CONFIRMED. `PawnSafe.Classify`:\n  `if (guest != null \u0026\u0026 guest.IsPrisoner) return guest.HostFaction != null \u0026\u0026 guest.HostFaction.IsPlayer ? ClassPrisoner : ClassPrisonerOther;`\n  and `FilterClasses` maps `\"prisoner\"` to `ClassPrisoner`.\n- `cc8988c`'s finish-off step and its \"right default TODAY only because there is\n  no prison\" caveat — CONFIRMED, quoted accurately.\n- 3.3 (`1adc737`) is open and `acee526` (1.9) does declare \"BLOCKS 3.3\".\n  CONFIRMED. **But the issue's parenthetical \"3.3 (rooms/beds)\" is too generous:**\n  3.3's scope is `build {def}` + `place-layout`. A bed can be PLACED by 3.3;\n  nothing in 3.3 marks it `ForPrisoners`. The dependency is incomplete — the\n  prison-room work needs a bed-ownership verb that NO FILED ISSUE currently owns.\n  That is the concrete thing to file when this placeholder becomes a spec.\n  (`1adc737`'s own acceptance has the same gap from the other side: its\n  \"Room role=Bedroom\" bullet cannot pass without an owned bed, and there is no\n  verb to own one. Same missing verb, two issues.)\n\n=====================================================================\nVANILLA MECHANICS, FOR WHOEVER WRITES THIS UP\n=====================================================================\n\n- **The causal direction is BED -\u003e ROOM, not room -\u003e bed.** `Verse/Room.IsPrisonCell`\n  is a plain cached field (`public bool IsPrisonCell =\u003e isPrisonCell;`),\n  recomputed in `Room.Notify_RoomShapeChanged`:\n  `isPrisonCell = false; if (Building_Bed.RoomCanBePrisonCell(this)) { ... containedAndAdjacentThings[i] is Building_Bed { ForPrisoners: not false } ... }`.\n  `Building_Bed.RoomCanBePrisonCell` is `if (r.ProperRoom) { return !r.IsHuge; } return false;`.\n  So \"make a prison\" means \"put a prisoner bed in a proper, non-huge room\", not\n  \"mark a room\".\n- `Room.Notify_RoomShapeChanged` FORCE-WRITES BACK:\n  `if (Current.ProgramState == ProgramState.Playing \u0026\u0026 isPrisonCell) { foreach (Building_Bed containedBed in ContainedBeds) { containedBed.ForPrisoners = true; } }`\n  — you cannot have a mixed room, and this is another route into the `= true`\n  setter.\n- The ROLE is separate and scored: `RoomRoleWorker_PrisonCell.GetScore` returns\n  `170000f` for exactly one non-medical prisoner bed and `0f` the moment any\n  humanlike bed in the room has `!ForPrisoners`; `RoomRoleWorker_PrisonBarracks`\n  handles two or more.\n- `Pawn_GuestTracker.SetGuestStatus` BURNS THE SHARED RAND STREAM —\n  `float num = pawn.kindDef.initialResistanceRange.Value.RandomInRange;`,\n  `resistance = GenMath.RoundRandom(num);`, and `will = ... initialWillRange.Value.RandomInRange`\n  — two to three draws per call, plus `DropAndForbidEverything()`,\n  `ClearMind_NewTemp(...)`, `health.surgeryBills.Clear()` and\n  `AddAndRemoveDynamicComponents`. Both current callers are `dev:*` and journalled,\n  so it is legal today; a PLAYER verb reaching it would be a determinism hazard of\n  the `_mp/DETERMINISM.md` class.\n- **`dev:guest-status` does not produce an identical-to-capture prisoner.** The\n  real capture path is `JobDriver_TakeToBed.CheckMakeTakeePrisoner` -\u003e\n  `Takee.guest.CapturedBy(Faction.OfPlayer, pawn)`, and `CapturedBy` wraps\n  `SetGuestStatus` with `HomeFaction?.Notify_MemberCaptured`, a\n  `TaleDefOf.Captured` tale, a `RecordDefOf.PeopleCaptured` increment and a\n  reachable `\"LetterLabelUnrecruitablePawnCaptured\"` letter. Fine for a fixture,\n  wrong if a test asserts on the letter or on goodwill.\n- Provider names, for citation accuracy: it is\n  `RimWorld/FloatMenuOptionProvider_CapturePawn` (and `_CaptureEntity`), not\n  `FloatMenuOptionProvider_Capture`; `FloatMenuOptionProvider_Arrest` is correct.\n  `PawnOrderVerbs.TakeToBedGate`'s `case \"capture\":` already reproduces\n  `CapturePawn`'s two gates (`clickedPawn.CanBeCaptured()` and\n  `HealthAIUtility.CanRescueNow(..., forced: true)`) plus the two-pass\n  `RestUtility.FindBedFor` search. Nothing to redo.\n- One more red-error path for any prison-room verb:\n  `Verse/GridsUtility.IsInPrisonCell` (used by `GenAI.CanBeArrestedBy`) does\n  `Log.Error(\"Checking prison cell status of \" + intVec + \" which is not in or adjacent to a room.\")`.\n\n=====================================================================\nACCEPTANCE\n=====================================================================\n\nThere is none, and that is CORRECT and correctly self-declared — the issue says\nit is \"scoped as a placeholder with the reasoning captured, not a spec ready to\ndispatch\", which is consistent with CLAUDE.md's \"the Acceptance section is the\ndefinition of done\". Nothing to assess. Three things must land in it when written:\n\n1. The \"does a prison exist?\" read is ALREADY SHIPPED — assert against\n   `rooms[].prison_cell` / `rooms[].role == \"PrisonCell\"`, do not build a new read.\n2. The prison-bed write must not go through `SetBedOwnerTypeByInterface` and must\n   not write `ForPrisoners = false`, or it fails zero-red-errors and the\n   never-force-pause invariant on its first call.\n3. The dependency list needs a BED-OWNERSHIP verb that 3.3 does not scope and no\n   issue currently owns.\n\n=====================================================================\nWHAT I AM INFERRING, NOT CONFIRMING\n=====================================================================\n\n- That no filed issue owns bed ownership. I checked the open list and 3.3's scope\n  line; I did not read every closed issue.\n- That `Notify_RoomShapeOrContainedBedsChanged` is the right thing for a bed verb\n  to call by hand. That follows from where vanilla calls it, but I did not trace\n  every caller.","files":null}]}